## 1. Setup Memory MCP Integration

To enable your AI agent (Claude Desktop, Cursor) to read and write to the knowledge graph `memory.json`, you must configure the official Memory MCP server.

### A. Claude Desktop
Add to your `%APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json` (Windows) or `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json` (macOS):
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "project-memory": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-memory"],
      "env": {
        "MEMORY_FILE_PATH": "<absolute_path_to_this_repository>/memory.json"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### B. Cursor IDE
1. Go to **Settings -> Features -> MCP**.
2. Add new MCP server:
   - Name: `project-memory`
   - Type: `command`
   - Command: `npx -y @modelcontextprotocol/server-memory`
3. Launch Cursor with the environment variable set to the absolute path of your `memory.json`:
   - PowerShell: `$env:MEMORY_FILE_PATH="<absolute_path_to_this_repository>/memory.json"; cursor .`
   - Cmd: `set MEMORY_FILE_PATH=<absolute_path_to_this_repository>/memory.json && cursor .`

